{
  "id": "Lyo.Geolocation.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Geolocation.Postgres",
  "area": "Core",
  "tagline": "PostgreSQL persistence for canonical geolocation data using Entity Framework Core.",
  "description": "PostgreSQL persistence for canonical geolocation data using Entity Framework Core.\n\n**Archetype A (Lyo domain).** Vendor clients such as [`Lyo.Google.Geolocation.Client`](../../../Integration/Google/Lyo.Google.Geolocation.Client/README.md) persist via\n`IGeolocationStore` in the host. See [package layout](../../../docs/package-layout.md).",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Usage",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddPostgresGeolocationStoreFromConfiguration(configuration);"
    }
  ],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Overview",
      "text": "Schema `geolocation` holds `address` (canonical normalized addresses from `Lyo.Geolocation.Models.Address`) and `address_source` (provenance per import: `source_entity_*` + `imported_at`, owner `address_id`, lookup index on `source_entity_*`). There is no `geocode_cache` table. This project references only `Lyo.Geolocation`, `Lyo.Geolocation.Models`, and `Lyo.EntityReference.Postgres`. Not Google, Endato, or other vendors."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "Usage",
      "items": [
        "Call a vendor client (e.g. Google Maps) in a separate integration assembly.",
        "Map to `Address` + `EntitySourceRecord.From(externalRef, importedAt)` on `Sources`. Owner id is set on save.",
        "`await store.SaveAddressAsync(address, ct)` or `GetBySourceAsync` (queries `source_entity_*`) for idempotent ingest."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Migrations",
      "text": "Schema: `geolocation`. Design-time: `GEOLOCATION_CONNECTION_STRING` env var."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "See also",
      "text": "[`Lyo.Geolocation`](../Lyo.Geolocation/README.md)"
    }
  ],
